# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Project: NURSFPX Platform
**Date:** June 2026  
**Document Version:** 1.0  
**Status:** Approved  

---

## 1. Project Overview
The objective is to develop a proprietary web platform (**NURSFPX.com**) to host an initial library of **2,195+ academic documents**. Moving away from third-party ecosystems like Course Hero, this platform will serve as a high-trust, brand-building vehicle and a high-converting lead-generation engine for custom, bespoke academic assistance.

---

## 2. Information Architecture & Navigation
The platform's frontend will enforce a rigid, 3-tier hierarchical structure designed for intuitive user browsing and optimal SEO indexation.

```
[Level 1: Homepage] 
       │
       ▼
[Level 2: Class Category Page] 
       │
       ▼
[Level 3: Assignment / Document Page]
```

### 2.1 Level 1: Homepage (University Selection)
The root landing page will act as a routing portal, featuring prominent entry points for six primary institutional silos with their respective document allocations:
* **Capella University** (104 documents)
* **University of Phoenix (UOP)** (776 documents)
* **University of Arizona Global Campus (UAGC)** (839 documents)
* **Trident University** (287 documents)
* **Columbia Southern University** (27 documents)
* **Southern New Hampshire University (SNHU)** (162 documents)

### 2.2 Level 2: Class Category Page
Upon selecting a university, the user is presented with a clean, searchable index of specific course codes mapped to that institution (e.g., `COM-FPX 3700`, `PSYCH/650`, `BHA-FPX 4102`).

### 2.3 Level 3: Assignment/Document Page
The final node of the hierarchy displays individual assessments (e.g., *Assessment 1, Assessment 2, Assessment 3*). This page serves as the primary organic search landing page, hosting specific assignment instructions to capture high-intent traffic.

---

## 3. Functional Requirements

### 3.1 Content Management System (CMS)
* **Instruction Extraction & Rendering:** The CMS must ingest and display official assignment instructions/prompts (e.g., *"Theoretical Conceptualization Training Guide"*) to act as highly indexable SEO lead magnets.
* **Dynamic Metadata Engine:** Page titles (`<title>`), meta descriptions, H1 tags, breadcrumbs, and internal navigation elements must populate dynamically based on the current `University -> Course -> Assignment` matrix.
* **Standardized Layout Layouts:** A unified CSS/UI template system must be applied across all 2,195+ pages. While the layout structure remains rigid, subtle UI theme elements (e.g., accent borders or subtle color cues) should shift to align with the selected university's branding archetype.

### 3.2 Security & Digital Rights Management (DRM)
* **Obfuscation & "No-Copy" Scripting:** Implement frontend technical blocks including disabling right-click context menus, disabling standard text selection/highlighting (`user-select: none`), and intercepting common keyboard shortcuts (`Ctrl+C`, `Cmd+C`, `Ctrl+U`) to protect on-page copy from scraping.
* **Gated Solution Architecture:** Official prompt instructions are entirely public for SEO purposes. However, the actual completed, high-scoring solution document must be strictly hidden behind a lead-generation wall. No direct download links or plaintext solution content should exist in the client-side DOM.

### 3.3 Lead Generation & Conversion Optimizations
* **Omnipresent Floating Contact Anchor:** A persistent header or floating sidebar must continuously display direct human channels:
    * **Email:** Contact@nursfpx.com
    * **Phone:** (612) 208-2686
* **High-Intent Call-to-Actions (CTAs):** Every Level 3 assignment page must prominently display contextual banners offering a **"Custom, AI-Free, and Plagiarism-Free"** version of that exact paper.
* **Anonymity & Privacy Assurances:** Micro-copy must be embedded near all conversion points to alleviate student anxiety regarding data privacy, institutional compliance, and discretion.

